The quorum of the general assembly is one third of the members present, as established by the amendment of 2 May 2026. Where the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies.

The general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present[[cite:obs-0fea77438fbfe3945c0fd4e4af8f4005c2b0c0b2 "The general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present."]].

The bylaws state that the general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present[[cite:obs-8760f71804a123ef0787db970f414207f7b783c7 "The general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present."]].